course: dictionary
lesson: 5363
title: Kip: one word, three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one the writer means. In «I'm going for a kip», kip means a sleep or nap, because that fits the sentence. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
explain: Kip is slang, a relaxed word people use in Britain, Ireland and Australia. Here kip is a verb: to kip means to sleep, especially somewhere other than your own bed. «Kip down» means to sleep somewhere for the night, such as on a sofa.
explain: Callum, a keeper from Newcastle, «kipped» for six hours, and the word tells you he slept. Kip can also be a noun, the money of Laos, a country in Asia. When two meanings seem possible, read the sentence again and pick the one that fits.
fact: Kip is slang: a relaxed word for a sleep or a nap, used in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: «Have a kip», «grab a kip» and «kip down» are all ways of saying sleep or nap.
fact: «Kipped» is the past tense of kip: «Callum kipped for six hours.»
fact: In Ireland, a kip can also mean a dirty, messy, horrible place.
fact: The kip is also the money of Laos, a country in Asia.
exercise: «I'm going for a kip after lunch.» What does kip mean here? | A football match | A long walk | A big dinner | *A sleep or nap
exercise: Callum «kipped» for six hours before he played. What does kipped mean? | Shouted | Ate | Ran | *Slept
exercise: In a geography lesson, someone says «The kip is the money of Laos.» What is a kip here? | A dirty room in Ireland | *The money of Laos | A type of bread | A Scottish hill
test: Mum says, «Grab a kip on the sofa, you look shattered.» What does grab a kip mean? | Buy a snack from the shop | Clean the kitchen floor | *Have a short sleep | Run a fast race
test: In Ireland, someone says, «Your room is a kip!» What do they mean? | *It is dirty and messy | It is very large and bright | It is fresh and new | It is the money of Laos
exam: Read this: «Mum said, "Kip down on the sofa, love, and I'll wake you for tea."» What does kip down mean? | Pay for the sofa | Sit very still and quiet | *Sleep somewhere for the night, like on a sofa | Clean under the cushions
